{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b> מורבכת (תביאנה)</b> — in gematria: רתחין (roasters), that roast it (the oven) thoroughly, all its needs."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The word מורבכת does not appear in the standard Masoretic text of Leviticus 6:14; the parenthetical תביאנה is also not found in the verse. The term מורבכת may refer to a rabbinic baking/roasting term or may reflect a variant reading. The gematria and argument have been translated hyper-literally as the passage is textually obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:53.969503493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}